# Banter in Hartsblight Forest (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is hartsblight_forest): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ hb_pine_barrens_01_rook_lucan
if name:rook_coldwake and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:hb_pine_barrens and not flag.gorthos_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Mind the turf, Lucan, there is rusted iron laid under the needles without a single notice posted. At least the pines are planted in regulation straight lines.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Look at the trapper's stamp on the jaw. Poor craftsmanship, worse concealment, and a dreadful posture on the spring.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Your hound is stood by that pine with the empty leash tied round it. Tell him to settle down before he puts a paw in the hardware.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush now, Barnaby, the dark has teeth enough without you fretting over an old rope. Come back to my boots, someone left their dog behind a long time ago.
endif
-> END

~ hb_infested_outcrop_02_tobin_silas
if name:tobin_hayward and name:silas_vane and at:hb_infested_outcrop and not flag.gorthos_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Every beetle in the parish is chewing at the edge of this outcrop, Silas, yet not one crosses into the smoke. Even my lapels have gone quiet.
interject name:silas_vane: That hissing bottle on the rock is still paying out protection, friend, though the poor sods on the log folded early. Tell's in the twitch, and nothing here is twitching.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That trench is scored with raw acid and the soil is turned up soft all round the stone. If I step into that smoke, at least there is no spark in the pit.
interject name:silas_vane: Easy now, Tobin, I'll walk the rim between you and the fire pit while you check the sagging tent. Just don't ask me to pocket the bloated fellow's boots.
endif
-> END

~ hb_noxious_hollow_03_delphine_cordelia
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:cordelia_skein and at:hb_noxious_hollow and not flag.gorthos_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: White-green mould from root to canopy, Cordelia, and not a single clean spot to rest a hem. Even the stag carved into the beech looks underfed.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Fascinating pathology on the shelf fungus, darling, the way it splits the dead bark along the grain. You can almost hear my eyes clicking from across the hollow.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness is pulling faces at the trapper's torn pack, which means the joke inside is either rotten or half-eaten. Save the applause, I am not reading a damp journal.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Leave the paper to me, Delphine, and mind your cuff near the beech root. Whatever opened his thorax had very poor table manners and no sense of ratio.
endif
-> END

~ hb_patient_commune_04_rook_delphine
if name:rook_coldwake and name:delphine_ravelle and at:hb_patient_commune and not flag.gorthos_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Eighteen still in the grass, Delphine, and no stone or seal put over a single one of them. Even the well has gone white round the rim.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Mind the seams, darling, the spores are coming down like cheap paper snow under a bad spotlight. That drumming in the trees has no rhythm at all.
interject name:rook_coldwake: The docket here is plain enough. Look at those four under the one blanket, tucked in together before the rot took the garden.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Don't look at the little ones, Rook, just keep that brass knocker of yours quiet while we pass the pen. Even the sunflowers have their heads down tonight.
endif
-> END

~ hb_druid_commune_05_rook_cordelia
if name:rook_coldwake and name:cordelia_skein and at:hb_druid_commune and not flag.gorthos_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Burrowing out rotten trunks for dwellings is a textbook subsidence hazard, Cordelia, and the drainage across this common is non-existent. Half the doors have mouldy bedding spilled over the sill.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Do hold still, Rook, the spore density in this air is thick enough to coat your lungs, if you were using them. You have forgotten to breathe again since we passed the broken prayer rings.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Much obliged, I will mark the sigh down on the shift log once we clear the drum circle. Someone left gourd-and-bone instruments lying out on the wet stone.
interject name:cordelia_skein: And antler idols arranged with surprising symmetry, darling, though the humours of this whole clearing smell of damp marrow. Keep your ledger tucked dry under your shield.
endif
-> END

~ hb_altar_of_rot_06_delphine_tobin
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:tobin_hayward and at:hb_altar_of_rot and not flag.hb_effigy_burned
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Now that is stagecraft, Tobin, a towering branch lady with a hollow face and a full house of little stick extras. Though why the small ones are facing the back wall is beyond me.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Because you don't look a blight in the eye when you're woven out of dry twigs, Delphine. The weave on her ribs is tight, I'll give them that, even with the fungus taking her cheek.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: He says the stag on the stones is waiting for an encore, and he doesn't even have eyes. Look at the poor beast's head, turned as if it still hears the hounds.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You're fraying at the wrist just looking at those little stick dolls. Nobody brings a match near this glade while I'm stood in it, rot or no rot.
endif
-> END

~ hb_wellspring_07_lucan_tobin
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:tobin_hayward and at:hb_wellspring and not flag.gorthos_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, Tobin, a ceiling of live fungus sixty feet overhead, and a river the colour of tallow. Even the black reeds by the bank appear to be eavesdropping on our boots.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Worse than eavesdropping, Lucan, the taproot of this whole valley is soured right down to that churning green pool. Those standing stones are leaning like rotten teeth in a bad jaw.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Prime specimen of a pustule glowing on the bank, though I must deduct points for the odour of boiled turnip. Barnaby is keeping well behind my heel, and there is not a cloud of thunder in earshot.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Tell the little lad to stay off the wet moss by the water's edge. And whatever is stewing in that wellspring would blister a hound's pads clean off.
endif
-> END

~ hb_druid_commune_08_cordelia_tobin
if name:cordelia_skein and name:tobin_hayward and at:hb_druid_commune and flag.gorthos_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: The spore viscosity in the common has dropped by half since Gorthos fell, Tobin. My crimson thread actually hangs straight in the air instead of clotting on the breeze.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Right, the drumming is done, and the rot in these burrowed trunks has stopped creeping for an hour. Still smells of sour bedding and broken discipline, mind you.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Your pulse is much steadier than it was by the stones, darling, and that primrose on your cuff has opened a fraction. Shall I chart the calibration before we leave the hollow?
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep your glass vials to yourself, girl, my seams are tied off well enough for the walk back. Let these poor hollowed trees sit in the quiet without us poking the bark.
endif
-> END
